{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Abraham.</b> The addition of the letter resh: avir hamon goyim (\"father of a multitude of nations\"). The Name did not come to remove a letter from his name, but only to add." "And Sarah is a general descriptive name, unlike Sarai. And blessed be HaShem, to whom belong the foreknown decrees, who preceded and commanded Abraham to be circumcised before Sarah conceived, so that his seed would be holy."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {0 "Resolved הרי\"ש as 'the letter resh' from the Hebrew abbreviation."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:44:49.302340227Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}